{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both ground pins on each isolated CAN transceiver are connected to the same GND net.",
      "expected": "The transceivers’ primary and bus-side grounds should remain separate for the specified CAN galvanic isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND ... U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The shared ground defeats galvanic isolation, allowing ground-loop and common-mode disturbances to pass between the CAN bus side and the board.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["R34", "R35", "SW6"],
      "pins": ["R34.1", "R34.2", "R35.1", "R35.2", "SW6.1", "SW6.2", "SW6.3", "SW6.4"],
      "nets": ["/CAN0_N", "/CAN0_P", "/CAN1_N", "/CAN1_P", "Net-(R34-Pad2)", "Net-(R35-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The two 120-ohm resistors connect /CAN0_N to SW6.1 and /CAN1_N to SW6.2; the other switch pair connects /CAN1_P to SW6.3 and /CAN0_P to SW6.4. Closing the corresponding DIP switches therefore couples the two CAN buses rather than terminating each bus across its own P/N pair.",
      "expected": "If these are termination switches, each should connect a 120-ohm resistor across the P and N lines of its own CAN bus, while keeping CAN0 and CAN1 separate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_N ... R34.1(1,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_N ... R35.1(1,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(2,passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_P ... SW6.3(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_P ... SW6.4(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R34 | 120R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R35 | 120R"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With the switches closed, the CAN interfaces are coupled together and are not independently terminated; this can cause bus loading, communication errors, or unintended interaction between the two networks.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files connect both sides of each isolated CAN transceiver to common ground, defeating the specified galvanic isolation. The CAN switch and 120-ohm resistor wiring also appears to couple the two CAN buses instead of providing per-bus termination."
}

